        "name": "geocode_location",
        "description": "Convert a place name into geographic coordinates (lat,lon) and a canonical display name. Use this before calling eventSearch when the user names a place (e.g. \"Brooklyn\", \"Austin\", \"Toronto\"). Pass a bare city or place name; \"City, State\" strings are less reliable than the name alone. It does simple city-name matching and can't disambiguate a borough/neighborhood/metro — if a name resolves to an unexpected or far-off city (e.g. \"Manhattan\" → Manhattan, KS), retry with the parent CITY the user means (e.g. \"New York\"); re-sending the same name returns the same result.",
