      {
        "name": "my_tickets",
        "description": "Look up the signed-in user's tickets across past and upcoming events.\n\nTwo modes:\n1. Browse — leave `event_ids` empty. Use `filter` (upcoming/past/all) and optional `query` for free-text search across event title, performer, and venue. Returns a summary list.\n2. Lookup — pass `event_ids=[N, …]`. Returns full per-event detail for each event the user has tickets to, plus an `unmatched_event_ids` list for the requested ids the user does NOT have tickets for. Pass a single id to drill into one event; pass several to intersect against owned tickets (e.g. when joining a recommendations list).\n\nFull detail includes ticket groups with seat description, status, transferable/sellable flags, seat perks (text labels), order pricing (per-ticket + total), active listings, and outgoing transfers.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "properties": {
            "query": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null,
              "title": "Query"
            },
            "filter": {
              "default": "upcoming",
              "enum": [
                "upcoming",
                "past",
                "all"
              ],
              "title": "Filter",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "event_ids": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "items": {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "type": "array"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "default": null,
              "title": "Event Ids"
            },
            "limit": {
              "default": 20,
              "title": "Limit",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          "title": "_my_ticketsArguments",
          "type": "object"
        },
